  "paper_id": "ccs-2023-txphishscope-towards-detecting-and-understanding-transac-a32c4b01",
  "title": "TxPhishScope: Towards Detecting and Understanding Transaction-based Phishing on Ethereum",
  "abstract": "The prosperity of Ethereum attracts many users to send transactions and trade crypto assets. However, this has also given rise to a new form of transaction-based phishing scam, named TxPhish. Specifically, tempted by high profits, users are tricked into visiting fake websites and signing transactions that enable scammers to steal their crypto assets. The past year has witnessed 11 large-scale TxPhish incidents causing a total loss of more than 70 million.",
  "abstract_source_id": "src-abstract-ccs-2023-a32c4b01",
